__: 158cm [Profile (Arts Vision)](https://www.artsvision.co.jp/talent/14244/) | [Twitter](https://twitter.com/lynn_0601_) | [Instagram](https://www.instagram.com/lynn.06.01) Non-Anime Roles:','https://s4.anilist.co/file/anilistcdn/staff/large/n118806-2aFjOHv08Iwm.jpg'),(1640,'Daisuke Hiramaki','[Twitter](https://twitter.com/i/user/5825282)','https://s4.anilist.co/file/anilistcdn/staff/large/n134794-Guo2PVhTyBBe.jpg'),(1641,'Tomoyo Takayanagi','[Twitter](https://twitter.com/tomoyo_t_1014)','https://s4.anilist.co/file/anilistcdn/staff/large/n122320-tV8CERbhYcNV.png'),(1642,'Naomi Oozora','[Profile (Aoni Pro)](https://www.aoni.co.jp/search/ohzora-naomi.html) | [Twitter](https://twitter.com/osorasan703) | [Instagram](https://www.instagram.com/osorasan703/) | [Wiki (en)](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Naomi_Ōzora) | [Wiki (jp)](https://ja.wikipedia.org/wiki/大空直美) Naomi Oozora is a Japanese voice actress from Osaka Prefecture. In June 2012, she made her voice actor debut as a child in [Saint Seiya Omega](https://anilist.co/anime/12929). In January 2014, Oozora first starring role as [Inari Fushimi](https://anilist.co/character/74317) in [Inari, Konkon, Koi Iroha](https://anilist.co/anime/20488). On May 25, 2023, she announced on Twitter that she had married that February to a man she met and dated from last year, and that she is pregnant.','https://s4.anilist.co/file/anilistcdn/staff/large/n117329-b0JyOtyttcJI.jpg'),(1643,'Momoko Seto','[Twitter](https://twitter.com/mmk_seto)','https://s4.anilist.co/file/anilistcdn/staff/large/n298582-wQG1c3x4Mej8.jpg'),(1644,'Houchuu Ootsuka','Houchuu Ootsuka is a Japanese voice actor and narrator affiliated with the talent management firm Crazy Box. He is best known for his roles as the voices of: - [__Kyao Mirao__](https://anilist.co/character/15496) in [___Heavy Metal L-Gaim___](https://anilist.co/anime/2598) - [__Yazan Gable__](https://anilist.co/character/16807) in [___Zeta Gundam___](https://anilist.co/anime/85) - [__Chibodee Crocket__](https://anilist.co/character/1401) in [___G Gundam___](https://anilist.co/anime/96) - __Signalman__ in ___Gekisou Sentai Carranger___ - [__Deneb__](https://anilist.co/character/43203) in ___Kamen Rider Den-O___ - [__Melan Blue__](https://anilist.co/character/22831) in [___Brigadoon___](https://anilist.co/anime/1450) - [__Jiraiya__](https://anilist.co/character/2423) in…','https://s4.anilist.co/file/anilistcdn/staff/large/n95337-NnvEQEBKV2dR.jpg'),(1645,'Ayano Shibuya','[Twitter](https://twitter.com/shibuya_ayanono)','https://s4.anilist.co/file/anilistcdn/staff/large/n131242-5GS0lQor8BXe.png'),(1646,'Takehiro Miura','[Twitter](https://twitter.com/miuratakehiro) Affiliated with [CygamesPictures](https://anilist.co/studio/6182/). Currently lives in Saitama, was born in Tokyo and raised in Hyogo Prefecture. Went to Kobe Design University, however dropped out, after which he joined XEBEC. Later left XEBEC to pursue video games, where he worked as an artist and an illustrator. Upon meeting Masami Oobari at a Comiket he moved to studio G-1. He stayed with studio G-1 for 6 years, working on various anime projects. He was primarily an assistant animation director and key animator. Afterwards he returned to freelance work as an artist and illustrator yet again. While he was rarely seen in anime until recently, he has gradually begun to appear as a key animator and animation director from then on.','https://s4.anilist.co/file/anilistcdn/staff/large/n112071-0QidrCO1uTzG.png'),(1647,'Yumi Uchiyama','[Profile](https://osawa-inc.co.jp/women/uchiyamayumi/) | [Twitter](https://twitter.com/yuumin_uchiyama) On January 1st, 2025, it was announced that she had gotten married to voice actor [Yuusuke Kobayashi](https://anilist.co/staff/118407). • Tera Isezaki in \"Marco & The Galaxy Dragon\" (VG) (Japanese) • Natasha in \"Honkai: Star Rail\" (VG) (Japanese)','https://s4.anilist.co/file/anilistcdn/staff/large/n106784-reDoHBLWxi7J.jpg'),(1648,'Ai Kakuma','[Website](https://mausu.net/talent/kakuma-ai.html) | [Twitter](https://twitter.com/aimausu) Kakuma is voice provider for the VOCALOID Rana, who debuted in VOCALOID3. **Non-Anime Roles:**','https://s4.anilist.co/file/anilistcdn/staff/large/n113511-F58Tk4OFKs1w.jpg'),(1649,'Haruka Shiraishi','[ToysFactory Profile](https://www.toysfactory.co.jp/artist/harukashiraishi/) | [Blog](https://ameblo.jp/shiraishi-haruka/) | [Twitter](https://twitter.com/shiraharu48?s=09) Haruka Shiraishi is a Japanese actress and voice actress. She was previously affiliated with Hirata Office, but is currently affiliated with Toy\'s Factory.','https://s4.anilist.co/file/anilistcdn/staff/large/n112629-U0y9a5Z9ogfk.png'),(1650,'Yuuki Takada','[Profile (mausu)](https://mausu.net/talent/takada-yuuki.html) **Non-Anime Roles:**','https://s4.anilist.co/file/anilistcdn/staff/large/n119154-sWANDEExAuVD.jpg'),(1651,'Ryousuke Shibuya','[Twitter](https://twitter.com/shibu_cat)','https://s4.anilist.co/file/anilistcdn/staff/large/n134727-vJAwtuIwXVf1.jpg'),(1652,'Aoi Tada','[Official Website/Profile (SSP)](http://ssp-create.com/tadaaoi/) | [Twitter](https://twitter.com/tada_aoi) | [YouTube](https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCuAkxJn7ZlqVOLdiRQIeJVA) | [Wiki (jp)](https://ja.wikipedia.org/wiki/多田葵) | [Wiki (en)](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Aoi_Tada) Aoi Tada is a Japanese singer and former voice actress. She formerly belonged to Gekidan Himawari. Her most noted voice role is [Ed](https://anilist.co/character/16/) in [Cowboy Bebop](https://anilist.co/anime/1/). She also performed an insert song to the series, \"Wo Qui Non Coin.\" In March 2005, she signed on to Moon-Bunny Entertainment and began her singer-songwriting career.','https://s4.anilist.co/file/anilistcdn/staff/large/n95658-paHKYOWkhoOd.png'),(1653,'Unshou Ishizuka','[Profile (Aoni)](https://www.aoni.co.jp/search/ishizuka-unsho.html) | [Wiki (en)](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Unshō_Ishizuka) | [Wiki (jp)](https://ja.wikipedia.org/wiki/石塚運昇) A Japanese actor, voice actor, singer, narrator and theater director from Katsuyama, Fukui, Japan. Ishizuka was known for his deep, strong voice and was often cast in the role of older mature male characters, such as [Jet Black](https://anilist.co/character/3/) in [Cowboy Bebop](https://anilist.co/anime/1/), [Job Truniht](https://anilist.co/character/19474/) in [Legend of the Galactic Heroes](https://anilist.co/anime/820/), [Van Hohenhaim](https://anilist.co/character/9792/) in [Fullmetal Alchemist: Brotherhood](https://anilist.co/anime/5114/) and [Joseph Joestar](https://anilist.co/character/6356/) in [JoJo\'s…','https://s4.anilist.co/file/anilistcdn/staff/large/n95357-umndcceko65h.png'),(1654,'Norio Wakamoto','[Wiki (jp)](https://ja.wikipedia.org/wiki/若本規夫) Used to work for the Tokyo Metropolitan Police Department Riot Police. Voice Actor of Corvus/Dark Corvus in Epic 7','https://s4.anilist.co/file/anilistcdn/staff/large/n95084-RTrZSU38POPF.png'),(1655,'Kenyuu Horiuchi',NULL,'https://s4.anilist.co/file/anilistcdn/staff/large/262.jpg'),(1656,'Gara Takashima','[Profile](https://www.aoni.co.jp/search/takashima-gara.html) | [Wiki (jp)](https://ja.wikipedia.org/wiki/高島雅羅) Married to voice actor [Banjou Ginga](https://anilist.co/staff/95330/). **Non-Anime Roles:**','https://s4.anilist.co/file/anilistcdn/staff/large/n95497-ZisMmeLQfZr7.png'),(1657,'Shinichirou Watanabe','Most known for directing critically and commercially successful series, [Cowboy Bebop](https://anilist.co/anime/1/) and [Samurai Champloo](https://anilist.co/anime/205/). He is noted for blending together multiple genres in his anime. For example, in Cowboy Bebop, classic cowboy western mixes with \'60s/\'70s New York City film noir, jazz/blues music, Hong Kong action movies, and to top it off the series is set in space. In his later work, Samurai Champloo, he unites the cultures of Okinawa, hip hop, modern-day Japan, and chanbara.','https://s4.anilist.co/file/anilistcdn/staff/large/n97009-4K1Wc7JG9iLR.png'),(1658,'Erino Hazuki','[Twitter](https://twitter.com/2016aquamarine) | [Instagram](https://www.instagram.com/eri.sea10618/)','https://s4.anilist.co/file/anilistcdn/staff/large/n95585-q5noKAfKT13Z.png'),(1659,'Chinami Nishimura','[Profile (81produce)](https://www.81produce.co.jp/actor_search/index.php/item?cell003=%E3%81%AA%E8%A1%8C&cell029=%E5%A5%B3%E6%80%A7&keyword=&cell028=&cell004=&name=%E8%A5%BF%E6%9D%91%E3%80%80%E3%81%A1%E3%81%AA%E3%81%BF&id=264&label=1) | [Twitter](https://twitter.com/china_alfafa)','https://s4.anilist.co/file/anilistcdn/staff/large/n95553-m1IIC7sNSQ2h.png'),(1660,'Tomoko Kawakami','Tomoko Kawakami was a Japanese voice actress. Having graduated from the Toho Gakuen College of Drama and Music, she was affiliated with Production Baobab at the time of her death. In August 2008, Kawakami was diagnosed with ovarian cancer, which required surgery. During a three-year battle with cancer, most of her ongoing roles were replaced by other voice actresses, although the latter was able to do some voice work until her retirement in the start of the 2010s decade. She died on June 9, 2011 at the age of 41.','https://s4.anilist.co/file/anilistcdn/staff/large/n95071-bmS9MxvAdsTr.png'),(1661,'Junichi Satou','[Twitter](https://twitter.com/satojumichi) | [Wiki (jp)](https://ja.wikipedia.org/wiki/佐藤順一) Junichi Satou is a Japanese anime director, best known for working on shoujo-based anime and in the magical girl genre. He was formerly associated with [TYO Animations](https://anilist.co/studio/333/), formerly known as [Hal Film Maker](https://anilist.co/studio/34/). Satou’s first major work was directing the first, and a portion of the second season of [Sailor Moon](https://anilist.co/anime/530/) for [Toei Animation](https://anilist.co/studio/18/), after which he handed the position over to [Kunihiko Ikuhara](https://anilist.co/staff/100082/), although he continued to storyboard and direct episodes for the later seasons.','https://s4.anilist.co/file/anilistcdn/staff/large/n99002-OQBPLNU1ZcoV.png'),(1662,'Noriko Hidaka','[Website](https://norikohidaka.com/) | [Twitter](https://twitter.com/nonko_hidaka531) | [Instagram](https://www.instagram.com/nonko_hidaka531/) | [YouTube](https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCAKD48ecL5cR87BWPze34HQ) A Japanese actress, voice actress, singer and narrator. She played Minami Asakura in Touch, Akane Tendo in Ranma ½, Satsuki Kusakabe in My Neighbor Totoro, Near in Death Note, Seta Sōjirō in Rurouni Kenshin, Jean Roque Raltique in Nadia: The Secret of Blue Water and Kikyo in Inuyasha. She is also the dub actress for Jayma Mays in the American TV series Glee, as well as in The Smurfs film series. - Mysterious Voice - Metaphor: ReFantazio (VG) - Peritya - Girls\' Frontline 2: Exilium. (VG)','https://s4.anilist.co/file/anilistcdn/staff/large/n95181-VZKOK4WN0UuO.png'),(1663,'Mikako Komatsu','[Profile](http://www.hirata-office.jp/talent_profile/woman/mikako_komatsu.html) | [Artist Profile](https://www.toysfactory.co.jp/artist/mikakokomatsu/) | [Website](https://www.hirata-office.jp/komatsu_mikako/) | [Twitter](https://twitter.com/mikakokomatsu) | [Instagram](https://www.instagram.com/mikako_komatsu/) A Japanese voice actor affiliated with Hirata Office. She married fellow voice actor [Tomoaki Maeno](https://anilist.co/staff/96489/Tomoaki-Maeno) on May 12, 2020.','https://s4.anilist.co/file/anilistcdn/staff/large/n105071-Hcj0X2gcliPq.png'),(1664,'Kouji Yusa','He was married to voice actor [Kanako Mitsuhashi](https://anilist.co/staff/95546/Kanako-Mitsuhashi) but they divorced on June 2012. On October 15, 2026, it was announced that he married voice actress [Miyari Nemoto](https://anilist.co/staff/238272).','https://s4.anilist.co/file/anilistcdn/staff/large/n95068-AbL4cVGlYaM8.jpg'),(1665,'Keiichi Sonobe','[Profile (81 Produce)](https://www.81produce.co.jp/actor_search/index.php/item?id=70) | [Wiki (en)](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Keiichi_Sonobe) | [Wiki (jp)](https://ja.wikipedia.org/wiki/園部啓一)','https://s4.anilist.co/file/anilistcdn/staff/large/n96302-LV7xdQBELja3.png'),(1666,'Yuuji Ueda','[Wiki (jp)](https://ja.wikipedia.org/wiki/うえだゆうじ)','https://s4.anilist.co/file/anilistcdn/staff/large/n95058-fGnId7E4tgx3.jpg'),(1667,'Shinichirou Ueda','Shinichirou Ueda is a Japanese Actor and Voice Actor','https://s4.anilist.co/file/anilistcdn/staff/large/n116011-jLCBGdnG6K2I.png'),(1668,'Satoshi Mikami','**[Profile (nexeed)](https://www.nexeed.com/actor/Satoshi_Mikami)** Japanese actor and voice actor from Tokyo. He is best known for being the official Japanese dubbing voice of English actor Benedict Cumberbatch, including voicing the actor\'s roles as Dr. Stephen Strange (Marvel Cinematic Universe) and Sherlock Holmes (SHERLOCK). - Albus Batlin - Metaphor: ReFantazio (VG) - Gallagher - Honkai: Star Rail (VG)','https://s4.anilist.co/file/anilistcdn/staff/large/n118511-htoA4dCjugsd.jpg'),(1669,'Daisuke Kishio','[Twitter](https://twitter.com/daisacusacu) | [Profile](https://www.aoni.co.jp/search/kishio-daisuke.html) **Non anime roles** - Brant - Wuthering Waves (VG)','https://s4.anilist.co/file/anilistcdn/staff/large/n95440-j4iWV0MGWtBh.png'),(1670,'Youko Hikasa','[Agency Profile](https://inari-inc.com/talent/yoko-hikasa/) | [Blog](https://ameblo.jp/hikasayoko-official) | [Instagram](https://www.instagram.com/hikasayoko_official/) | [Threads](https://www.threads.net/@hikasayoko_official) | [(Old) Twitter](https://twitter.com/hikasayokoSP) Co-hosted the popular weekly radio show Odoroki Sentai Momonoki Five (おどろき戦隊モモノキファイブ) with fellow seiyuu [Eriko Nakamura](https://anilist.co/staff/103983) from 2009 to 2017. She got married to a person from outside the industry in 2015. On September 5, 2024, she announced that she was starting her own voice talent agency, [i.nari](https://inari-inc.com/), which would also be representing her going forward.','https://s4.anilist.co/file/anilistcdn/staff/large/n102263-aaPZtNXVUljW.jpg'),(1671,'Yousuke Saitou','Date of Birth: January 10 Place of Birth: Gifu Prefecture, Japan A stage actor affiliated with Herringbone.','https://s4.anilist.co/file/anilistcdn/staff/large/n168361-hltmE3Jeiz1i.jpg'),(1672,'Fukujurou Katayama','[Twitter](https://twitter.com/fukujuro)','https://s4.anilist.co/file/anilistcdn/staff/large/n118706-wsgOB1xtoNB0.png'),(1673,'Yousei Bun',NULL,'https://s4.anilist.co/file/anilistcdn/staff/large/n118707-nEUtqpJKrvIz.jpg'),(1674,'Shunsuke Sakuya','[Twitter](https://twitter.com/398Syun) Non anime roles: - Osamu Kashiwagi - Yakuza/Like a Dragon series (VG)','https://s4.anilist.co/file/anilistcdn/staff/large/n102492-pQ40ldxp1aXB.png'),(1675,'Subaru Kimura','[Profile](https://www.atomicmonkey.jp/jp/archives/talent/kimurasubaru) | [Twitter](https://twitter.com/GiantSUBAru) | [Instagram](https://www.instagram.com/richpotatoboya/?hl=en) A German–Japanese actor, voice actor and narrator affiliated with talent agency [Atomic Monkey](http://www.atomicmonkey.jp/jp/), his best-known role is voicing Takeshi Goda in the Doraemon series, which has spawned numerous specials.','https://s4.anilist.co/file/anilistcdn/staff/large/n107480-h2RgLXNP7hcj.png'),(1676,'Yuusaku Yara','[Wiki (jp)](https://ja.wikipedia.org/wiki/屋良有作)','https://s4.anilist.co/file/anilistcdn/staff/large/n100770-UwcMoND5FIgC.png'),(1677,'Masako Nozawa','- (1997) Won the \"Special/Lifetime Achievement\" Award at the 2nd Kobe Animation Awards. - (2006-04-01) Resigned from 81 Produce and established her own office, Office Nozawa.','https://s4.anilist.co/file/anilistcdn/staff/large/n95557-5a2nnIBK05ul.png'),(1678,'Masaaki Yuasa','[Twitter](https://twitter.com/masaakiyuasa) An acclaimed anime director known for his wild, freeform style. After graduating from the Kyushu Sangyo University\'s Faculty of Arts in 1987 he joined studio [Ajia-do](https://anilist.co/studio/30/Ajiado), initially as in-betweener but rapidly moving to key animation. In the first part of his career Yuasa established himself as an idiosyncratic creator while working on several child friendly anime, such as [Chibi Maruko-chan](https://anilist.co/anime/951/Chibi-Marukochan/) and [Doraemon](https://anilist.co/anime/2677/Doraemon-Nobitas-Animal-Planet/), but especially on [Crayon Shin-chan](https://anilist.co/anime/966/Shin-Chan/), a project he was involved with for most of the \'90s.','https://s4.anilist.co/file/anilistcdn/staff/large/n100068-6DCiwXuyBESm.png'),(1679,'Yuu Hayashi','[Twitter](https://twitter.com/voice_singing) Yuu Hayashi is a Japanese voice actor and singer affiliated with Ken Production. Formerly a child actor, he mainly specializes in dubbing roles. He is a vocalist of [SCREEN Mode](https://anilist.co/staff/119992/), a band signed with Lantis. - Billy Kid - Zenless Zone Zero (VG) - Merold - Fragaria Memories (Multimedia Project) - Issei Hoshino - Judgment, Lost Judgment (Videogames)','https://s4.anilist.co/file/anilistcdn/staff/large/n116157-MAPYgEeptEUh.png'),(1680,'Toshiki Masuda','**Height:** 176 cm (5\'9) [Website](https://www.toshikimasuda.jp/) | [Twitter](https://twitter.com/ToshikiMasuda38) | [Instagram](https://www.instagram.com/toshi.m38/) | [Youtube](https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCx47ourWgyHf3iAl77MYY0g/featured) - Rover - Wuthering Waves (VG) - Masayoshi Tanimura - Yakuza 4 Remastered','https://s4.anilist.co/file/anilistcdn/staff/large/n107017-Jv96B9DBJOy9.png'),(1681,'Shiori Mikami','[Profile](https://www.aoni.co.jp/search/mikami-shiori.html) | [Twitter](https://twitter.com/mikami_shiori) | [Blog](https://ameblo.jp/mikami-shiori/) | [Blog (old)](http://blog.livedoor.jp/kirax2_day/)','https://s4.anilist.co/file/anilistcdn/staff/large/n106236-aGhlIhHPPtjc.png'),(1682,'Jun Shishido','Affiliated with [Mappa](https://anilist.co/studio/569/).','https://s4.anilist.co/file/anilistcdn/staff/large/n107494-I2FoE5ro29Zh.png'),(1683,'Akari Kitou','[Profile (Racoon Dog)](https://www.raccoon-dog.co.jp/talent/r09-kitou.html ) | [Official Site](https://kitoakari.com/) | [Twitter (Official)](https://twitter.com/kitoakari_staff/) | [Twitter (Personal)](https://twitter.com/kitoakari_1016/) | [Instagram](https://www.instagram.com/kitoakari_staff/) | [YouTube](https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCU_E2DHcyQu-Toohyd1vzRw) A Japanese voice actress. She debuted in 2014, got her first main role in *Time Bokan 24* (2016), and has since received more leading roles. On October 16, 2019, her 25th birthday, she made her debut as a solo music artist under Pony Canyon. After the agency Pro-Fit shut down their operations, she joined the new agency Racoon Dog on 2022.','https://s4.anilist.co/file/anilistcdn/staff/large/n119722-Ls7ORfBejJEP.jpg'),(1684,'Azusa Tadokoro','[Profile](https://inspion-agc.co.jp/ja/talent/tadokoro-azusa/) | [Twitter](https://twitter.com/AzusaTadokoro) | [Instagram](https://www.instagram.com/azusa_tadokoro/) | [YouTube](https://www.youtube.com/@koroazu_channel/) | [Facebook](https://www.facebook.com/tadokoroazusaofficial) | [Blog](https://ameblo.jp/azusa-tadokoro) When Azusa was in eighth grade, she was inspired to become a voice actress after hearing [Akiko Yajima](https://anilist.co/staff/95148/Akiko-Yajima)\'s performance as Kohaku in Inuyasha. She participated in Horipro\'s 36th Talent Scout Caravan on October 11, 2011, winning the event, and made her debut as a voice actress in 2012, voicing a character in a commercial for SSK Foods.','https://s4.anilist.co/file/anilistcdn/staff/large/n112297-seUP8O4obuYO.png'),(1685,'KAORI.','[Spunky Strider Official Blog](http://spunkystrider.jugem.jp) KAORI. is a Japanese voice actress and singer. Before 2000, she was known as Kawana Midori (川菜翠) and Kawana Akiko (川菜明子). \"KAORI\" is a portmanteau of Kawana Midori. She is a member of the rock band Spunky Strider.','https://s4.anilist.co/file/anilistcdn/staff/large/249.jpg'),(1686,'Yoshihisa Kawahara','[Blog](http://experimentalward.blog45.fc2.com/) - Ovis Gideaux - Metaphor: ReFantazio (VG)','https://s4.anilist.co/file/anilistcdn/staff/large/n95409-87S6L0u8gQNf.jpg'),(1687,'Aya Hirano','[Blog](http://ameblo.jp/hirano--aya/) | [Twitter](https://twitter.com/hysteric_barbie) | [Instagram](https://www.instagram.com/a_ya.hirano/) | [Website](http://ayahirano.jp/) Aya Hirano is a Japanese actress, voice actress, and singer. Beginning in the entertainment industry as a child actor performing in television commercials, she played her first voice acting role in 2001 in the anime television series [Angel Tales](https://anilist.co/anime/682/). She released her first single \"Breakthrough\" in 2006, and her first album Riot Girl in 2008. She was formerly contracted to Space Craft Produce, a branch of the Space Craft Group, before moving to the talent agency Grick in August 2011. Her label was Lantis until 2011, when she moved to Universal Sigma.','https://s4.anilist.co/file/anilistcdn/staff/large/n95004-qWQQHGzY3wqr.png'),(1688,'Morio Asaka','Asaka joined [Madhouse](https://anilist.co/studio/11/) after graduating from Osaka Designers\' College. There his first job was working as an assistant director for [Toshio Hirata](https://anilist.co/staff/117533/) on [Phoenix: Yamato Chapter](https://anilist.co/anime/2999/). Later he made his debut as an episode director on [Yawara!](https://anilist.co/anime/691/), and soon after as a director on [Pops](https://anilist.co/anime/2093). His notable works include [Cardcaptor Sakura](https://anilist.co/anime/232/), [Nana](https://anilist.co/anime/877/), [Chihayafuru](https://anilist.co/anime/10800/), and [My Love Story!!](https://anilist.co/anime/20946/) among others. Many of his works take on a female perspective for the telling of the story, with a feminine protagonist as the central focus.','https://s4.anilist.co/file/anilistcdn/staff/large/n100921-Sd0rSsSxxzpW.png'),(1689,'Kazuyuki Okitsu','**Height:** 175cm [Profile (Kekke)](http://www.kekke.co.jp/talent/male/ak/okitsu.html) | [Twitter](https://twitter.com/okitsu3__8) Kazuyuki Okitsu is a Japanese voice actor and narrator. After he graduated from the Osaka University of Arts he was initially represented by the REM talent agency but from May, 2007 he has been affiliated with Kekke Corporation. When he was a 3rd year high school student he was the moderator for the 79th Japanese High School Baseball Championship opening ceremony. - Lúcio (Overwatch) - Horropedia (Reverse: 1999) - Komano Manato (Zenless Zone Zero)','https://s4.anilist.co/file/anilistcdn/staff/large/n102288-xqcBKreDyZYN.png'),(1690,'Yuka Komatsu','[Profile](https://www.aoni.co.jp/search/komatsu-yuka.html) | [Twitter](https://twitter.com/soyyuka) | [Instagram](https://www.instagram.com/soyyuka?igsh=a3owZm40YTJyNnM4)','https://s4.anilist.co/file/anilistcdn/staff/large/n104858-ao0i80o81GHR.png'),(1691,'Masako Satou','Originating from [Studio Ghibli](https://anilist.co/studio/21/).','https://s4.anilist.co/file/anilistcdn/staff/large/n126654-xrmr6wjREsB0.png'),(1692,'Yuka Terasaki','[Profile (Oginext)](http://www.oginext.com/women/terasaki.html) | [Twitter](https://twitter.com/terachan0804) | [Instagram](https://www.instagram.com/terachan0804/) | [Blog](https://ameblo.jp/after-grow/)','https://s4.anilist.co/file/anilistcdn/staff/large/n95671-iXGq2oxE1DlW.png'),(1693,'Mitsuki Saiga','[Agency (Ken Production)](https://www.kenproduction.co.jp/talent/35) | [Twitter](https://twitter.com/SaigaTweet)','https://s4.anilist.co/file/anilistcdn/staff/large/n95197-4Uxn95bRlvMu.jpg'),(1694,'Kazuhiko Inoue','[Twitter](https://twitter.com/inouekazuhiko) | [Profile](http://www.b-box-box.com/actor/井上和彦/) | [Blog](https://ameblo.jp/kazufan/) | [Anison](anison.info/data/person/1055.html) | [Wiki (EN)](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kazuhiko_Inoue) | [Wiki (JP)](https://ja.wikipedia.org/wiki/%E4%BA%95%E4%B8%8A%E5%92%8C%E5%BD%A6_(%E5%A3%B0%E5%84%AA&#x29;) Kazuhiko Inoue is a Japanese actor, voice actor and narrator, who has become one of Japan\'s most well established voice actors since his debut in 1973.','https://s4.anilist.co/file/anilistcdn/staff/large/n95021-9qAoAn6GNZ3S.png'),(1695,'Sanae Kobayashi','[Instagram](https://www.instagram.com/sanae__kobayashi/) | [Agency Profile](https://sigma7.co.jp/actors/kobayashi_sanae) **Non-anime roles:** - Aile - Rockman ZX Advent (VG) - Akari Tatsushiro - Naruto Shippuden: Ryujinki (VG) - Akira Okuzaki - Mai-HiME: Bakuretsu! (VG) - Aleria - Final Fantasy Crystal Chronicles: Ring of Fates (VG) - Alex Russo - Wizards Of Waverly Place (Japanese dub) - Allen Walker - J-Stars Victory VS (VG) - Ashley Hammond/Yellow Ranger - Power Rangers in Space (Japanese dub) - Ashley Hammond/Yellow Ranger - Power Rangers Lost Galaxy (Japanese dub) - Cecilia Lynne Adlehyde - Wild Arms Alter Code: F (VG) - Charabom - Bomberman Generation (VG) - Constable Neyla - Sly 2: Band of Thieves (VG) - Dalia Hakbarah - You Don\'t Mess with the Zohan (Japanese dub) - Ender -…','https://s4.anilist.co/file/anilistcdn/staff/large/n95149-xNDmN92Feq8y.png'),(1696,'Kazuma Horie','[Blog](http://ameblo.jp/horie-kazuma/) | [Twitter](http://twitter.com/Kazuma_Horie)','https://s4.anilist.co/file/anilistcdn/staff/large/n95456-a2LdFNUAoJS3.png'),(1697,'Takahiro Oomori','[Twitter](https://twitter.com/t0mori)','https://s4.anilist.co/file/anilistcdn/staff/large/n101671-EmRY0EMXCafO.jpg'),(1698,'Tomohisa Hashizume','[Twitter](https://twitter.com/tomohisa0413)','https://s4.anilist.co/file/anilistcdn/staff/large/n110005-65qAMtTf7qOb.png'),(1699,'Satomi Akesaka','[Twitter](https://twitter.com/akekodao) | [Agency Profile](http://amuleto.jp/talents/AkesakaSatomi.html) | [Blog](http://blog.animate.tv/akesaka/) Satomi got her start in show business in 2001 when she won the \"Idol Grand Prix\", an idol contest sponsored by the manga magazine Nakayoshi. She became an event character for the anime \"Tokyo Mew Mew\" by joining the group Mew Five. She made her debut as a voice actress in 2004 in with role of Anzai Futaba from Koi Kaze, and as a stage actress a year later. She released her first single \"Akeban!\" in 2011.','https://s4.anilist.co/file/anilistcdn/staff/large/n95723-bV625Jngt5o6.png'),(1700,'Yuuki Itou',NULL,'https://s4.anilist.co/file/anilistcdn/staff/large/n121293-Q5NMkmJ3I6FP.jpg'),(1701,'Tetsuya Kakihara','[Profile](http://zynchro.jp/talent/kakihara.html) | [Instagram](https://www.instagram.com/charisma.tetsuya.days/) | [Blog](https://ameblo.jp/tetsuya-kakihara/) Commonly referred to as Kakkii by fans, Kakihara is a voice actor and a singer. As the latter, he is a member of Kiramune (music label) and represents the color of green. He was inspired to become a voice actor by [Yuuji Ueda](https://anilist.co/staff/95058/Yuuji-Ueda)\'s performance in the Tokimeki Memorial dating sim game, and moved from Germany to Japan at age 18 to pursue his dream. Kakihara speaks Japanese, English and German.','https://s4.anilist.co/file/anilistcdn/staff/large/n95167-wjIShzThRTlS.png'),(1702,'Yukari Fukui','[Blog](https://ameblo.jp/yukari-hukui/) | [Twitter](https://twitter.com/yukalyric)','https://s4.anilist.co/file/anilistcdn/staff/large/n95359-ZgCbzadpH4g4.png'),(1703,'Jouji Nakata','[Profile (Osawa Inc)](https://osawa-inc.co.jp/men/nakatajouji/) | [Twitter](https://twitter.com/joujinakata123)','https://s4.anilist.co/file/anilistcdn/staff/large/n95091-idoMaN26z80B.png'),(1704,'Nobuyuki Hiyama',NULL,'https://s4.anilist.co/file/anilistcdn/staff/large/n95257-PgYwsBplRSJa.png'),(1705,'Michiko Neya','[Wiki (en)](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Michiko_Neya) | [Wiki (jp)](https://ja.wikipedia.org/wiki/%E6%A0%B9%E8%B0%B7%E7%BE%8E%E6%99%BA%E5%AD%90) Michiko Neya is a Japanese voice actress. She formerly worked at Arts Vision but is now a freelancer. Non-anime roles:','https://s4.anilist.co/file/anilistcdn/staff/large/n95176-3yZnUwXap7nX.png'),(1706,'Hiroyuki Imaishi','[Twitter (shiimai)](https://twitter.com/shiimai) | [Sakugabooru](https://www.sakugabooru.com/post?tags=hiroyuki_imaishi+) Hiroyuki Imaishi was born in 1971, in Tokyo. He joined studio Gainax after graduating from Tama University of Arts. Imaishi later left the studio to establish his own studio, Trigger, where he still works to this day. Imaishi made a name for himself on *Hideaki Anno*\'s [Kareshi Kanojo no Jijou](https://anilist.co/anime/145/Kareshi-Kanojo-no-Jijou/). He did key animation and storyboards for several episodes, with episode 19 being a standout for its unorthodox paper cutout animation. His presence injected some stylized levity into Anno\'s shoujo drama.','https://s4.anilist.co/file/anilistcdn/staff/large/n97349-OG5UDDs1g0AI.jpg'),(1707,'METEOR','[Twitter](https://twitter.com/meteorfunkaratt) | [Instagram](https://www.instagram.com/meteorfunkaratt/)','https://s4.anilist.co/file/anilistcdn/staff/large/n224545-hYmDs9mgQDgT.png'),(1708,'Riho Iida','[Website](https://iida-riho.com/) | [Profile](https://www.houeishinsha.co.jp/h_detail_sptalent.cgi?OFFICE=T&KIND=1&ID=51efb7ec_6622) | [Blog](http://gree.jp/iida_riho/) | [Twitter](https://twitter.com/rippialoha) | [Instagram](https://www.instagram.com/rippi_ii/) | [YouTube](https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCx6-VxBUu65TR0PctsyQb8g) | [Niconico](https://ch.nicovideo.jp/rihoism) | [Wiki (en)](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Riho_Iida) | [Wiki (jp)](https://ja.wikipedia.org/wiki/飯田里穂) Riho Iida is a Japanese ex-child model-turned-actress, voice actress and singer.','https://s4.anilist.co/file/anilistcdn/staff/large/n112207-FZGGO2a34Wqt.png'),(1709,'Kenji Hamada','[Agency](https://mausu.net/talent/hamada-kenji.html) Married to voice actress [Junko Takeuchi](https://anilist.co/staff/95015) since 2006 and has two children. - Elphas Bardon - Metaphor: ReFantazio (VG) - Ben Bigger - Zenless Zone Zero (VG)','https://s4.anilist.co/file/anilistcdn/staff/large/n95371-nyA7w7nPrlPr.png'),(1710,'Souma Saitou','__[Website](https://www.saitosoma.com/) | [Blog](https://ameblo.jp/somasaito/) | [Profile (81produce)](https://www.81produce.co.jp/dcms_plusdb/index.php/item?cell003=%E3%81%95%E8%A1%8C&label=1&cell004=&name=%E6%96%89%E8%97%A4%E3%80%80%E5%A3%AE%E9%A6%AC&id=47) | [Twitter](https://twitter.com/SomaStaff)__ He started his singing career in 2017. Named Best Rookie Actor at the 9th Seiyu Awards (2015) and won the Singing Award at the 16th Seiyu Awards (2021). **Non-anime roles:**','https://s4.anilist.co/file/anilistcdn/staff/large/n113227-x0UXLNL6v08X.png'),(1711,'Koudai Sakai','[Profile](https://animoproduce.co.jp/artists/sakaikodai/)','https://s4.anilist.co/file/anilistcdn/staff/large/n119832-6UV28VP1MXWI.png'),(1712,'Baku Kinoshita','[Website](https://www.pics.tokyo/member/baku-kinoshita/) | [Twitter](https://twitter.com/mugicaan1) | [Instagram](https://www.instagram.com/mugicaan/) An animator and character designer currently working at animation studio P.I.C.S.','https://s4.anilist.co/file/anilistcdn/staff/large/n204553-BrPhPEdzkSpu.png'),(1713,'Takuya Igarashi','[Twitter](https://twitter.com/igarashi_takuya) Formerly part of [Toei Animation](https://anilist.co/studio/18/). Currently freelance with ties to studio [Bones](https://anilist.co/studio/4/).','https://s4.anilist.co/file/anilistcdn/staff/large/n105087-aoj9RdnTaZ45.png'),(1714,'Saki Fujita','[Blog](https://blog.goo.ne.jp/sakky-ohana) | [Twitter](https://twitter.com/sakitaf_1019) She is best known in Japan for sampling her voice for the Vocaloid, [Hatsune Miku](https://anilist.co/staff/110205/Miku-Hatsune).','https://s4.anilist.co/file/anilistcdn/staff/large/n95504-pDIKpd8t2EYU.png'),(1715,'Rina Satou','__[Profile (Haikyo)](https://haikyo.co.jp/profile/profile.php?ActorID=11916) | [Twitter](http://twitter.com/rinasatoh)__ - Guilty - Goddess of Victory: Nikke (VG) - Eula - Genshin Impact (VG) - USS California - Azur Lane (VG) - Caesar King - Zenless Zone Zero (VG) - Helena Martin - Reverse Collapse: Code Name Bakery (VG)','https://s4.anilist.co/file/anilistcdn/staff/large/n95241-4XvR64oguxwS.png'),(1716,'Miki Itou','[Profile](https://osawa-inc.co.jp/women/itomiki/)','https://s4.anilist.co/file/anilistcdn/staff/large/n95121-FCp9NcoFgKZk.png'),(1717,'Kotomi Deai',NULL,'https://s4.anilist.co/file/anilistcdn/staff/large/n118729-LDDoEMw